  "notes": "SOURCE: Official Minot State University catalog, Department of Nursing page (requirements only; Minot State publishes no official semester sequence for the pre-licensure BSN, so this is a requirements-only plan). CATALOG YEAR NOTE: the catalog site does not display an edition year; this is the current catalog as accessed 2026-10-10. The page publishes the degree as 122 credits; the itemized requirements sum to 112 (40 support + 9 support not required for admission + 63 post-admission), so a 10-credit General Education/Electives block is recorded to reach the published 122. Admission to the nursing major requires: minimum C in each required support course, 2.80 GPA in required support courses, 47 SH plus UNIV/FYE, minimum 8 required support courses including two sciences, and a proficient TEAS score. HMS 215 and HMS 243 must be completed prior to or concurrent with NURS 255/264; PSY 270 (min C) before NURS 354; statistics (min C) before or concurrent with NURS 363. Program is CCNE-accredited and approved by the ND Board of Nursing.",
